  "note": "Election of the restored Donaghadee Urban District Council (twelve members) after some years under a Commissioner. Fourteen candidates were nominated on 5 May 1936 (Belfast News-Letter, 6 May 1936, p. 9); Messrs. Matear [William Matier] and Adams [Albert John Adams] withdrew the next day, so there was no contest (Belfast Telegraph, 7 May 1936, p. 14). Filed on 15 May 1936, the 1936 polling day for urban councils; no poll. No poll: twelve candidates for twelve seats after two withdrawals. No party labels printed (the members were mostly Ratepayers' Association nominees). Returned unopposed."
